      "data": {
        "label": "Note",
        "id": "nG1",
        "params": {
          "text": "## Les imports à connaître\n\n```python\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import KNeighborsClassifier\nfrom sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression, LogisticRegression\nfrom sklearn.svm import SVC\nfrom sklearn.cluster import KMeans\nfrom sklearn.metrics import (accuracy_score, classification_report,\n                             ConfusionMatrixDisplay, r2_score)\n```\n\nTous les modèles s'utilisent de la même façon : `modele.fit(X_train, y_train)`, puis `modele.predict(X_test)` ou `modele.score(X_test, y_test)`.",
          "bg_color": "#1e293b",
          "text_color": "#cbd5e1"
        }
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 520,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nG2",
      "type": "canvas_note",
      "position": {
        "x": 710,
        "y": 4200
